The prior `t=6` exact top run timed out, while modular chart runs can still be useful. I’m letting the modular `t=7` top jobs hit their bounds; if they time out, I’ll switch to a more targeted finite-field approach that computes certificates row-subsystem by row-subsystem instead of asking for one monolithic basis.
